[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2576020281","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101241#issuecomment-2576020281","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101241","id":2576020281,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZivM5","user":{"login":"michaelharmonart","id":15620900,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjIwOTAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15620900?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart","html_url":"https://github.com/michaelharmonart","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaelharmonart/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-07T19:01:11Z","updated_at":"2025-01-07T19:01:11Z","body":"@BastiaanOlij I believe you might have an idea how this is setup and how I might work around it in the meantime?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2576020281/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3166116746","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101241#issuecomment-3166116746","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101241","id":3166116746,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68txuK","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-07T23:23:42Z","updated_at":"2025-08-07T23:23:42Z","body":"Thanks for the report!\n\n> With non-one scale on the origin node stereoscopic rendering is completely broken.\n\n`XROrigin3D` nodes aren't intended to be scaled - that's why there is `world_scale`. I don't know if this can be made to work, but I wouldn't consider it not working to be a bug, but a missing feature.\n\n> This is somehow reset each time I re-open the editor despite having saved the scene with a modified scale.\n\nI wonder if this is because we have a single global world scale on `XRServer`, but also a property on `XROrigin3D` that will update the world scale? Perhaps each time an `XROrigin3D` is created, it resets the world scale? Worth investigating\n\n> With non-one scale on the \"world scale\" property the XRCompositionLayer nodes are broken (incorrect placement)\n\nWhat do you mean by \"incorrect placement\"? What are you expecting to happen and what is happening?\n\nI'm not totally surprised that there are issues, though - we don't test `world_scale` very frequently","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3166116746/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3166283515","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101241#issuecomment-3166283515","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101241","id":3166283515,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68uab7","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-08T01:19:17Z","updated_at":"2025-08-08T01:19:17Z","body":"Indeed as David says, right now `world_scale` is the solution here, though obviously we need to look into the impact on composition layers (I suspect we just missed a step here).\n\nThat said, doing the scaling on `XROrigin3D` is something we've looked into various times as it \"feels right\" but everytime we've run into various edge cases where it actually does the wrong thing.\n\nI do want to revisit this in the future and figure out what we can do here that makes sense, but until that time `world_scale` is the solution we recommend.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3166283515/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]